 ```
 
-A failed delivery is not retried.
+`deliver` returns a `DeliveryResult` with `delivered` (true on a 2xx response), `status`
+(the last status code received) and `attempts` (one `Attempt` per request made, so
+`len(result.attempts)` is the attempt count).
+
+Each request times out after 5 seconds. Connection errors, timeouts and 5xx responses are
+retried up to 3 times (4 attempts in total) with exponential backoff of 1s, 2s and 4s.
+Any other response, including 4xx, is final and not retried. A delivery that still fails
+is reported through the result rather than raised. Only `http` and `https` URLs are
+accepted; anything else raises `ValueError`.
